{"title":"Alphabet in Motion: Artist Kelli Anderson’s Wondrous Pop-up Biography of the Letters","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/12/02/alphabet-in-motion-kelli-anderson/","date":1764707006000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img width=\"320\" height=\"418\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?fit=320%2C418&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"Alphabet in Motion: Artist Kelli Anderson’s Wondrous Pop-up Biography of the Letters\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?w=1098&amp;ssl=1 1098w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?resize=320%2C418&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?resize=600%2C783&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?resize=240%2C313&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion.jpg?resize=768%2C1002&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p><p>It is astonishing enough that we invented language, this vessel of thought that shapes what it contains, that we lifted it to our lips to sip the world and tell each other what we taste, what it is like to be alive in this particular sensorium. But then we passed it from our lips to our hands and gave it form so we can hear it with our eyes and see with our minds, making <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2011/06/21/shapes-for-sounds/\">shapes for sounds</a> and meaning from the shapes. </p>\n<p>We take it for granted now, this makeshift miracle permeating every substrate of our lives, and go on tasking these tiny concrete things with conveying our most immense and abstract ideas. We forget how young this technology of thought is, younger than <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/traversal/\">Earth’s largest living organism</a>, and yet it tells a richer story of who we are than any archeological artifact, touches more of what makes us human than the fossil record. Our letters carry the history of our species and of our world, their shapes shaped by a conversation between the creativity of our imagination and the constraints of our creaturely reality, from the rotational geometry of the human wrist to the chemistry of the first paints into which the first brushes were dipped. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.kellianderson.com/books/alphabetinmotion.html\" target=\"_blank\">Kelli Anderson</a>, maker of <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/tag/kelli-anderson/\">material magic</a>, brings that layered history to life in <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>Alphabet in Motion: How Letters Get Their Shape</em></strong></a> — a large-format two-volume marvel, many years and myriad prototypes in the making, full of paper pulleys and accordion delights that illustrate the biography of each letter. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=680%2C494&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"494\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?w=2000&amp;ssl=1 2000w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=320%2C232&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=600%2C436&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=240%2C174&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=768%2C558&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?resize=1536%2C1115&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion4.jpg?w=1360&amp;ssl=1 1360w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?resize=680%2C798&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"798\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?w=1000&amp;ssl=1 1000w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?resize=320%2C375&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?resize=600%2C704&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?resize=240%2C282&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion3.jpg?resize=768%2C901&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=680%2C551&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"551\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?w=2560&amp;ssl=1 2560w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=320%2C260&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=600%2C487&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=240%2C195&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=768%2C623&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=1536%2C1246&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?resize=2048%2C1661&amp;ssl=1 2048w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion6-scaled.jpg?w=1360&amp;ssl=1 1360w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=680%2C551&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"551\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?w=2200&amp;ssl=1 2200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=320%2C259&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=600%2C487&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=240%2C195&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=768%2C623&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=1536%2C1246&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?resize=2048%2C1661&amp;ssl=1 2048w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion5.jpg?w=1360&amp;ssl=1 1360w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Through a kaleidoscope of disciplines, from art and design to anthropology and history, Kelli shines a dazzling light on how we went from ink to lead to pixel, drawing on everything from Plato’s <em>Cratylus</em> to an 1882 textbook on the workings of the Jacquard loom to (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2014/12/10/ada-lovelace-walter-isaacson-innovators/\">sparked the concept of the first computer code</a> in the fertile mind of the the young Ada Lovelace) to the punch card revolution and its hidden history of women working under pseudonyms to conjure up the digital universe. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=680%2C789&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"789\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?w=1444&amp;ssl=1 1444w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=320%2C371&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=600%2C696&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=240%2C278&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=768%2C891&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion1.jpg?resize=1324%2C1536&amp;ssl=1 1324w\" /></a> </p>\n<p>In one of the wonderful short essays accompanying each letter, she writes:</p>\n<blockquote><p>For many cultures over time, the A’s triangular form has represented strength and stability. This association likely originated in the physical world. The triangle is is the most stable load-bearing shape because it distributes force and tension to either side of its wide base. In terms of physics, the majority of simple machines utilize the triangle’s intrinsic morphological power: the wedge, inclined plane, and lever all work thanks to their triangular forms.</p>\n<p>Long before physics provided a cogent explanation, early human civilizations had observed and utilized the structural strength of the triangle in their architecture and simple machines. By extension, for hundreds of years across the Hellenic world, the A was thought to have the power to curse and to heal, and regularly appeared in religious and medicinal rituals. The letter A neatly connected symbolic mysticism with the demonstrable power of the built world. (There exists a symmetry between “to spell” and “a spell.”)</p></blockquote>\n<p>Observing that “every letter has a long history,” Kelli traces the lineage of A:</p>\n<blockquote><p>The A we recognize today is the result of various cultures’ remapping of this shape to sights and concepts of local environments. </p>\n<p>The A’s triangular form begins in Egypt in 3100 BCE as a pictogram of a perched eagle, a bird central to ancient Egyptian religion.</p>\n<p>The more agrarian-minded Phoenicians transformed the eagle into <em>aleph</em> (from the Hebrew word for “ox”). Now rotated, this bovine appears in profile with its horns pointing to the right, its nose to the left. A vertical line defines the back of the ox’s head, which introduces the A’s horizontal crossbar.</p></blockquote>\n<p>One of the great blind spots of our cultural hindsight is the continuity of ideas — we look back and gasp at what appears as a breakthrough, failing to see its <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/08/22/margaret-boden-creativity/\">combinatorial nature</a>, the way everything builds on what came before. Kelli writes:</p>\n<blockquote><p>The word “text” comes from the Latin verb <em>texere</em>, which means “to weave” (hence the origin of an expression like “to spin a yarn”). Computers, which were first used for typesetting and are direct technological descendants of weaving, seem to perfectly bridge texere’s dual meanings. Weaving is a binary technology: Its vertical warp and horizontal weft (and the way those two components, together, render a yarn visible/invisible) are a precursor to how the 1s and 0s of today’s computers work. Woven binary code memory served as the rudimentary computer navigation system onboard the <em>Apollo 11</em> mission.</p></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion10.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Alongside the paper playground of ideas is a rigorously researched magazine chronicling the history of technology and the evolution of typography. What emerges is something thoroughly unexampled: part pop-up exploratorium, part encyclopedia, part wunderkammer with twenty-six compartments of wonder, part homage to the unsung heroes who, working in the shadow of their time and place, shaped the modern world. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?w=2000&amp;ssl=1 2000w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?resize=1536%2C1024&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion2.jpg?w=1360&amp;ssl=1 1360w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion7.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion8.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?resize=680%2C453&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"453\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?resize=320%2C213&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?resize=600%2C400&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?resize=240%2C160&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion9.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?resize=680%2C1019&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"1019\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?w=1001&amp;ssl=1 1001w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?resize=320%2C480&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?resize=600%2C899&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?resize=240%2C360&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/alphabetinmotion16.jpg?resize=768%2C1151&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Alphabet-Motion-Letters-Their-Shape/dp/0997175915/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>Alphabet in Motion</em></strong></a>, the tactile delight of which is thoroughly untranslatable onto a digital screen, lives in that rare place where imagination and illumination meet to become a portal of wonder — the gift of a lifetime. </p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"825b7eec8cddbf4f0016525f51a73539676c05efb43fadc4016da09dbebc9a30","category":"Sites"}